<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04RG">Example <span data-tag="04RG">10.1.2.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set and let $| S |$ denote its geometric realization as a topological space (Definition <a data-tag="001Y" href="/tag/001Y">1.2.3.1</a>). Combining Proposition <a data-tag="04QR" href="/tag/04QR">10.1.1.1</a> with Corollary <a data-tag="04RF" href="/tag/04RF">10.1.2.7</a>, we deduce that the homotopy type of the topological space $| S |$ depends only on the underlying semisimplicial set of $S$. Compare with Corollary <a data-tag="0125" href="/tag/0125">3.4.5.5</a>. </p>
